==English==

===Alternative forms===
* {{l|en|ambodexter#Noun}} {{lb|en|obsolete form}}

===Etymology===
Borrowed from {{bor|en|ML.|ambidexter}}, from {{der|en|la|ambi-}} + {{m|la|dexter}}.

===Pronunciation===
* {{IPA|en|/ambɪˈdɛkstə/|a=UK}}

===Noun===
{{en-noun}}

# Someone who is [[ambidextrous]].
# {{lb|en|archaic}} A lawyer who takes fees from both plaintiff and defendant.
#* {{RQ:Melville Billy Budd|text=But the thing which in eminent instances signalizes so exceptional a nature is this: though the man's even temper and discreet bearing would seem to intimate a mind peculiarly subject to the law of reason, not the less in his heart he would seem to riot in complete exemption from that law, having apparently little to do with reason further than to employ it as an '''ambidexter''' implement for effecting the irrational.}}
# {{lb|en|by extension}} Someone who is [[two-faced]]; a {{l|en|double-dealer}}, such as a {{l|en|cheat}} or a {{l|en|crook}}.
#* {{RQ:Burton Melancholy|edition=2nd}}, New York Review of Books, 2001, p.65:
#*: One takes upon him temperence, holiness&nbsp;[…], whenas indeed he, and he, and he, and the rest are hypocrites, '''ambidexters''', outsides, so many turning pictures, a lion on one side, a lamb on the other.

===Adjective===
{{en-adj|-}}

# [[ambidextrous|Ambidextrous]].
#* {{RQ:Smollett Peregrine Pickle|[http://www.gutenberg.org/files/4084/4084-h/4084-h.htm Chapter 100]|text=He then changed his battery, and being '''ambidexter''', raised such a clatter upon the turnkey’s blind side, that this hero, believing him left-handed, converted his attention that way, and opposed the unenlightened side of his face to the right hand of Pipes {{...}}}}

